<===> README.md
Checking whether a selector ending in `~` is a superselector of a selector
with a descendant combinator in the middle (no combinator) crashed libsass
(`.front()` on an empty combinator list), e.g. while trimming `@extend`.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> extend/input.scss
.a ~ .b, .a ~ .c .d {x: y}
.e {@extend .d}
<===> extend/output.css
.a ~ .b, .a ~ .c .d, .a ~ .c .e {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> function/child/input.scss
@use "sass:selector";
a {b: selector.is-superselector(".a ~ .b", ".a ~ .c > .d")}
<===> function/child/output.css
a {
  b: false;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> function/descendant/input.scss
@use "sass:selector";
a {b: selector.is-superselector(".a ~ .b", ".a ~ .c .d")}
<===> function/descendant/output.css
a {
  b: false;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> function/sibling/input.scss
@use "sass:selector";
a {b: selector.is-superselector(".a ~ .b", ".a ~ .c ~ .d")}
<===> function/sibling/output.css
a {
  b: false;
}
